# Everything here is regenerable by the scripts one directory up, and some of it must
# not be committed at all.
#
# Two prompt sets built from `likaixin/InstructCoder` carried third-party secrets — a
# Slack webhook and a Stripe test key that real GitHub code had leaked into that
# dataset — and GitHub's push protection blocked the branch until they were purged from
# history. Any regenerated code prompt set will trip it again, so the rule is that
# generated data does not go in git.
#
# The traces are the other reason: 16 rank traces at 10-14 MB each is 200 MB of clone
# weight whose value lasted exactly as long as the analysis that read them. Conclusions
# belong in `RESULTS.md`, `CURRENT-STATUS.md` and the handoff documents; the bytes do
# not belong here.
*
!.gitignore
# `cost-profile.json` is an input, not an artifact: the runners read it and write a
# per-run copy beside their own output.
!cost-profile.json
